# Shipyard CLI

[Shipyard](https://goshipyard.app) is a directory of AI-built apps, with a paid board
that finds threads where people are asking for what an app does. Drive it with the
`shipyard` CLI (public API at `https://goshipyard.app/api/v1`, authed by the user's
personal API key). Add `--json` to any command for parseable output.

## First, confirm auth

```sh
shipyard whoami            # prints @handle — if so, you're ready
```

- `command not found` → install: `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonnonz1/goshipyard/main/install.sh | sh`
- "Not authenticated" → user creates a key at https://goshipyard.app/account (API keys), then `shipyard login` (paste it). Never invent a key.

## Common tasks

```sh
# List an app (title, pitch, url required)
shipyard projects create -t "Foglight" -p "Maps for makers" -u https://foglight.app -c devtools --hero ./shot.png

# List / inspect / edit your listings
shipyard projects list --mine
shipyard projects get <id>                 # upvotes + reaction counts
shipyard projects update <id> -p "Sharper pitch"
shipyard projects delete <id> -y           # takes it down; an owner can put it back on the site

# Reactions — what people said (read-only)
shipyard reactions <id>

# Likes (upvotes) — idempotent
shipyard like <id>
shipyard unlike <id>

# The board (paid plan) — threads to answer, each with a suggested reply
shipyard opportunities list <id>
shipyard opportunities mark <card-id> posted --reply-url URL
shipyard opportunities mark <card-id> dismissed
```

## Rules

- Parse `--json`; don't scrape output. Non-zero exit = failure.
- Shipyard never posts for anyone, and neither do you. Show the user the thread and
  the suggested reply; they post it from their own account; then mark the card posted
  with the link to their reply.
- Preserve `review_source` when summarizing reactions: `seeded` or `member`. Seeded
  ones came from Shipyard's own seed accounts. Member is not proof of hands-on use.
  Missing provenance means unknown.
- Confirm public actions (listing, editing, taking down) with the user first.
- Never fabricate pitches, reactions or results — write from what was actually built.
- Don't bulk-like to game rankings.
- If the board needs a subscription, say so once: https://goshipyard.app/pricing.
- Local dev: pass `--api-url http://localhost:4001`.
- Help: `shipyard help` or `shipyard <command> help`.
- No CLI? A hosted MCP server exposes the same operations at
  `https://goshipyard.app/mcp` (add `Authorization: Bearer sk_live_…`). Setup:
  https://github.com/jonnonz1/goshipyard/blob/main/docs/mcp.md
- The CLI can upload local screenshots and take a listing down; MCP cannot.
